From f855149fb71b5a09bc7cd7c98df30d479f778594 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:28:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: map an HDR10+ picture by its own metadata and
 tone curve

An HDR10 or HDR10+ picture that the bridge maps to a display itself ("HDR10 and
HDR10+ adapted to the display", the mapping to SDR) was mapped by the static
HDR10 metadata of the stream: BT.2390 (or the spline) from the peak of the
mastering display, the same for every scene. The HDR10+ metadata of each
picture (SMPTE ST 2094-40) were not used, and neither was the tone curve that
the studio made for a display of a given peak.

struct dvbridge_plain now carries them (dvbridge_hdr10plus_map.h), as
dvbridge_hdr10plus_plain() takes them from FFmpeg's, checked against the
standard: application version 0 or 1, every value in its range, a targeted
display of 1 to 10000 cd/m2, at most 15 anchors (9 in version 1), and a curve
that never goes down (8.7.4, equation (2)). The mapping is then guided by the
scene: its brightest is the highest MaxSCL (or the last percentile of maxRGB,
B.3), given to libplacebo in all three components, and where the picture
carries a curve, the curve is libplacebo's pl_tone_map_st2094_40 with that
Bezier curve, on a table of 1024 entries. Without HDR10+ metadata nothing
changes: the same parameters, the same bytes.

Measured on Mesa's software OpenGL ES (llvmpipe and zink) against an
independent computation of ST 2094-40 8.7.4 (a neutral ramp of every 10-bit
code): on a display of the curve's target, 0.04 to 0.56 codes of 12-bit PQ at
most, 0.01 to 0.02 on average, in 21 curves and displays. Without HDR10+, the
same bytes as before in five mappings and both drivers. A frame costs the
same; the table is made again once a scene.

libplacebo takes the range of the curve as the luminance of the three MaxSCL
before it raises it to the highest, and caps the output peak by the former: a
display brighter than that luminance was mapped to it (1698 instead of 1783
cd/m2 in a measured case). Giving the brightest in all three avoids it.
